- op: discuss  # 98a1
  at: '2026-09-16T07:09:35Z'  # 98a1
  by: agent  # 98a1
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 98a1
  clock: 5  # 98a1
  nonce: 98a1  # 98a1
  message: "SATISFIED 2026-09-16 by PR #994 (9d552f3bd1) + PR #995 (5467d2ed00). Behavioral\nevidence, this item's own filed repro re-run on dev 5467d2ed00.\n\nTHE FILED REPRO. Appending a line to io_primitives/rust.yaml and running\nsmart-test --manifest:\n\n    before (as filed)   # Changed source files: 0   # Selected tests: 1\n    now                 # Changed source files: 0   # Selected tests: 158\n\nTHE RESIDUAL THIS ITEM WAS RE-SCOPED TO, closed by measurement. Every family\nthat selected ZERO on 2026-09-16, probed end to end by touching one real\nshipped file in each and reading the manifest:\n\n    frameworks          107 files    0 -> 59\n    dataflow_patterns    20 files    0 -> 41\n    cfg_nodes             5 files    0 -> 79\n    function_summaries    4 files    0 -> 12\n    taint_sources         2 files    0 -> 143\n    taint_sanitizers      1 file     0 -> 143\n    library_signatures    5 files    0 -> 8\n    url_folding           2 files    0 -> 7\n    io_primitives        15 files  157 -> 159\n\nThe last row is the control that matters: widening must not narrow, and it did\nnot.\n\nTHE MECHANISM. The grep terms are derived per family from\nhypergumbo_core.yaml_catalogs.YAML_CATALOGS -- the registry validate_registry()\nalready gates against the tree -- so the eleventh family arrives covered by the\ncommit that registers it. Three arms: the directory name, the loader module the\nregistry names, and the load_* entry points read out of that loader's source.\nThe loader arm is the load-bearing one and that is measured: the directory name\nalone reaches 58 test files, the union reaches 157. Families sharing a loader\nreach each other, which is what keeps the widening from narrowing the overlay\narm.\n\nA SECOND KEYED-TO-ONE-INSTANCE DEFECT, FOUND IN MY OWN FIX AND CLOSED BEFORE\nTHIS CLOSURE. The first cut keyed on YAML. This item's statement says \"a\nnon-Python input\", and url_folding/SCOPE.md is parsed by get_scoped_languages()\non every run that folds a URL -- it selected nothing. The key is now \"not\nPython\" rather than \"is YAML\": SCOPE.md 0 -> 7 tests. Eight files, but the\nshape was the same one level down.\n\nDISCLOSED, NOT CLOSED BY THIS. Test selection for CI CONFIG is a different\nstatement and stays open under INV-lizor: nothing in smart-test claims\n.woodpecker/, yet 15 root tests read it, so a change to ci.yml runs none of its\nown gates."  # 98a1
